# SAT is a no-op for a third model: tri3 is worse than its own tri2, and the
# speaker-independent pass ties it exactly on test (15.70, same error count).
#
# Chain test errors, best LM weight per system:
#   Base L9        209 ins / 164 del / 452 sub = 825
#   Large L14      174 ins / 203 del / 451 sub = 828
#   mms-300m L14   174 ins / 157 del / 404 sub = 735
# mms-300m wins on all three error types, so this is an acoustic gain and not a
# better insertion/deletion operating point. Note that model size is not the
# variable: mms-300m (~300M) and HuBERT Large (~317M) are the same scale, yet
# Large only ties Base. What differs is pretraining data, ~491k hours across
# 1400+ languages against 60k hours of English audiobooks.

# Monotone improvement from 10 to 13, then flat: 13 and 14 are within noise of
# each other and swap ranks between dev and test. So the phonetic quality of
# Large is still rising at 14, not past its peak, and the layer choice does not
# explain why Large fails to beat Base. Probing upward (16, 18, 20) is the
# open question. Experiment dirs: exp_hubert_large_l{10,11,12,13}.
# Experiment dirs from both runs are kept as exp_hubert_base_l9 /
# exp_hubert_large_l14 (likewise pca_* and run_ssl_*.log).

